Good afternoon,

Flock Organization and Network Audits are not exempt from public disclosure; in fact, they are intended for public disclosure. Per Flock Safety's "Guide to Flock Safety Data for Open Records Laws":

"The audit logs can be accessed via your agency's Flock admin dashboard on the 'Insights' tab. These logs may show the date/time of search, user ID, and search parameters and reason. Customers may download these logs in the user interface as spreadsheets in 31-day increments. It is recommended that Flock customer support assist customers with the downloads when feasible for timeframes larger than six months and major accounts."

The cited Georgia Code applies to data obtained from automated license plate recognition systems, not to the audit logs generated by use of the system. I am not requesting ALPR data, I am requesting the organization and network audit logs that record the system's use. As indicated in the above quote, this includes but is not limited to:
1. Records of license plate searches performed by agency personnel;
2. Timestamps of searches;
3. User identification information (names, badge numbers, or user IDs);
4. Any associated case numbers or investigation references.

Best,
a
